                <pb facs="1054" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg958"/>

                <head>No. 644.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to General Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 23,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Have telegraphed to Borne for authority to Italian minister to take custody of
                    library and property.</p>
                <p>Spanish government, through minister here, proposed arbitration, which has been
                    declined on the ground that the question is not one for arbitration, the subject
                    being one of national honor., of which the nation must be the judge and
                    custodian.</p>
                <closer><signed>FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
